{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "37571246",
      "title": "Computed Values & Effects",
      "lectureOrder": 682,
      "videoOrder": 627,
      "sourceHash": "1656a494874503626c63b6518b0f8fef18ab2acd2b5d694b8f518315b140a6a5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.11,
          "en": "Now, to conclude this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.11,
          "end": 8.49,
          "en": "there are just two additional features which already exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.49,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "in Angular and which I also wanna mention.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 15.453,
          "en": "And the first one would be the computed function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.44,
          "end": 20.373,
          "en": "which you also can import from Angular Core.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.21,
          "end": 23.85,
          "en": "And computed then takes a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.85,
          "end": 28.35,
          "en": "as a value and you must pass a function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.35,
          "end": 31.47,
          "en": "And it's a function that does not take any input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.47,
          "end": 34.38,
          "en": "but a function that should then return a value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.38,
          "end": 38.31,
          "en": "typically a value that's based on other signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 38.31,
          "end": 41.61,
          "en": "For example, here we could read the counter signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 41.61,
          "end": 43.413,
          "en": "and multiply it with two.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.94,
          "end": 48.6,
          "en": "And computed exists to give you an easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 48.6,
          "end": 52.17,
          "en": "of creating well, computed values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 52.17,
          "end": 55.62,
          "en": "So values that depend on other values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.62,
          "end": 59.22,
          "en": "other signal values to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.22,
          "end": 61.53,
          "en": "So here, doubleCounter would now be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 61.53,
          "end": 65.31,
          "en": "by Angular whenever this counter signal changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 65.31,
          "end": 69,
          "en": "and only then, and doubleCounter then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69,
          "end": 72.21000000000001,
          "en": "of course, could also be used here in your template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 72.21000000000001,
          "end": 75.15,
          "en": "You would use it like a signal, so you would execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 75.15,
          "end": 76.263,
          "en": "as a function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 77.16,
          "end": 80.13,
          "en": "Angular would also memorize that doubleCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.13,
          "end": 81.69,
          "en": "is being used here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 81.69,
          "end": 84.21000000000001,
          "en": "and it would understand that doubleCounter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 86.7,
          "en": "uses the normal encounter as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 86.7,
          "end": 90.63,
          "en": "So as a value inside of function and Angular, therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.63,
          "end": 95.63,
          "en": "recomputes doubleCounter whenever this counter changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 100.233,
          "en": "and then updates the UI whenever doubleCounter changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 101.49000000000001,
          "end": 104.46000000000001,
          "en": "So Angular watches for all these changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.46000000000001,
          "end": 108.39,
          "en": "And therefore, computed gives us a smart and easy way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 108.39,
          "end": 112.89,
          "en": "of computing values that depend on other signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 112.89,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "And with that here, you see that the counter now indeed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 117.963,
          "en": "is basically doubled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 119.16,
          "end": 122.55,
          "en": "The last signal-related feature I also want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.55,
          "end": 127.35,
          "en": "to introduce here is another function provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.35,
          "end": 129.183,
          "en": "The effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.68,
          "end": 133.65,
          "en": "Now, effect is a function that could be executed here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 133.65,
          "end": 136.32,
          "en": "in the constructor, though you're not limited",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.32,
          "end": 137.57999999999998,
          "en": "to the constructor.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 137.57999999999998,
          "end": 140.16,
          "en": "You could also use it in other places,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 140.16,
          "end": 142.98,
          "en": "for example, in the NgOn init method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 142.98,
          "end": 146.57999999999998,
          "en": "But here I'm using the constructor, and effect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 146.57999999999998,
          "end": 150.3,
          "en": "just like computed takes a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.3,
          "end": 152.793,
          "en": "So again, this must be a function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.63,
          "end": 154.65,
          "en": "In this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 154.65,
          "end": 159.09,
          "en": "you can now also use signals, but the idea behind effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 159.09,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "is not to produce a new value, but instead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 166.71,
          "en": "to run code whenever a signal changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 166.71,
          "end": 170.43,
          "en": "So for example, here I can console.log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.43,
          "end": 172.89,
          "en": "the current counter value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.89,
          "end": 175.38,
          "en": "and as always, counter must be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.38,
          "end": 176.64,
          "en": "as a function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 176.64,
          "end": 179.733,
          "en": "because that's how you read a signal value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 180.6,
          "end": 182.649,
          "en": "So effect therefore allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 182.649,
          "end": 186.99,
          "en": "to define code that depends on signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 186.99,
          "end": 191.1,
          "en": "And Angular will automatically re-execute this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 191.1,
          "end": 193.29,
          "en": "that's being passed to effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.29,
          "end": 195.898,
          "en": "and therefore, this code here, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.898,
          "end": 199.32,
          "en": "whenever any signal being used inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.32,
          "end": 201.24,
          "en": "of this function changes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 201.24,
          "end": 202.38,
          "en": "So in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 202.38,
          "end": 207,
          "en": "Angular understands that this code uses this counter signal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 207,
          "end": 210.9,
          "en": "and whenever this counter changes, and only then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.9,
          "end": 214.233,
          "en": "Angular will go ahead and re-execute this code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 215.34,
          "end": 218.1,
          "en": "Therefore, if you save this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 218.1,
          "end": 220.2,
          "en": "and you open your developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 220.2,
          "end": 223.59,
          "en": "you also see the counter being output there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 223.59,
          "end": 226.083,
          "en": "That's coming from this effect function.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
